## L11, 2026-10-24: a kept-copy tar line for a box without a box repo, carried by docs/backups.md "A rebuilt box" in PR #356 until the owner dropped the recipe the same day (the guide's way back is the box repo); a record, not guidance. On Debian 13, dev container
 Container motel-dev-run-016a8ffd374f Creating 
 Container motel-dev-run-016a8ffd374f Created 
Debian GNU/Linux 13 (trixie)
tar (GNU tar) 1.35
$ find etc/motel | sort
etc/motel
etc/motel/Caddyfile
etc/motel/age
etc/motel/age.pub
etc/motel/age/identity
etc/motel/agenda.env
etc/motel/demo.env
etc/motel/deploy.key
etc/motel/deploy.key.pub
etc/motel/secrets
etc/motel/secrets/demo.env
$ umask
0022
$ sh -c 'umask 077; tar --exclude=motel/age --exclude=motel/age.pub -czf /root/etc-motel.tar.gz -C /etc motel'   (paths under $d)
$ tar -tzf /root/etc-motel.tar.gz
motel/
motel/secrets/
motel/secrets/demo.env
motel/deploy.key
motel/agenda.env
motel/Caddyfile
motel/demo.env
motel/deploy.key.pub
$ stat -c "%A %a %U:%G %n" /root/etc-motel.tar.gz
-rw------- 600 root:root /root/etc-motel.tar.gz
## the after-an-attack extraction as the guide prints it: the same archive, deploy.key* left out of the extraction
$ sudo tar -xzf etc-motel.tar.gz -C /etc --exclude="motel/deploy.key*"   (the guide quotes the pattern with single quotes; here -C $d/new, no sudo)
$ find new/motel | sort
new/motel
new/motel/Caddyfile
new/motel/agenda.env
new/motel/demo.env
new/motel/secrets
new/motel/secrets/demo.env
$ stat -c "%A %a %n" new/motel/secrets new/motel/secrets/demo.env
drwxr-xr-x 755 new/motel/secrets
-rw-r--r-- 644 new/motel/secrets/demo.env

## L11b: a bare debian:13 image — what apt brings with backblaze-b2, restic and rclone
$ dpkg -l ca-certificates (before)
un  ca-certificates <none>       <none>       (no description available)
$ apt-get install -s backblaze-b2 | grep -A1 "additional packages" | grep -c ca-certificates   # 1 = brought in
1
$ apt-get install -s restic | grep -A1 "additional packages" | grep -c ca-certificates   # 1 = brought in
0
$ apt-get install -s rclone | grep -A1 "additional packages" | grep -c ca-certificates   # 1 = brought in
0
$ apt-cache depends --recurse --no-recommends --no-suggests --no-conflicts --no-breaks --no-replaces --no-enhances backblaze-b2 | grep -c "^ca-certificates"
1
$ apt-cache depends rclone | grep -i cert
  Suggests: ca-certificates
$ apt-cache depends restic | grep -i cert
(none)
